%% Sequence Diagram — Login flow — Logical level
%% UC-11 Authenticate
%% Updated: 2026-05-22 (lifelines = logical components, messages = business actions —
%% no class names, no BCrypt/JWT/HS256 specifics, no SQL)

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant V as Login screen (Client)
    participant API as Authentication API (Server)
    participant AUTH as Authentication rules
    participant STORE as User account storage

    U->>V: Enter username and password
    V->>API: Submit credentials
    API->>AUTH: Authenticate this user
    AUTH->>STORE: Find user account by username
    STORE-->>AUTH: User account (stored password digest, role)
    Note over AUTH: Compare the submitted password<br/>with the stored digest.<br/>If it matches, issue an access token<br/>that carries the user role.
    AUTH-->>API: Access token + role + display name
    API-->>V: Login successful
    V-->>U: Save token, redirect to dashboard

    Note over V,API: Every later request carries this token.<br/>The server checks the token and identifies<br/>the current user before serving the request
